SUMMARY:Poles and Plants
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an educational hike about plants and hiking poles!\nDuring this hike you’ll join TLC Trail Guide\, Nancy\, to learn how and when to set the length of your poles\, the most efficient way to grip your poles\, and how to decide what features you want in your hiking poles. We will have loaner poles for you to try thanks to Great Outdoor Provision Company and LEKI\, but if you have a pair already\, please bring them!\n\nAlong the way\, TLC Trail Guide\, Dale\, will point out local tree and plant species you will see throughout the preserve. This is a great hike to build on both your hiking pole and plant ID skills! This will be a moderate 2-3 mile hike over variable terrain\, stopping periodically for educational moments.  This is a free event\, but preregistration is required.\n\n \n\n\n\n\nIf registration for this event is full\, please fill out our waitlist form here\, by September 24th at noon. \n 
URL:https://triangleland.org/event/poles-and-plants-3
LOCATION:Johnston Mill Nature Preserve\, 2713 Mt. Sinai Rd.\, Chapel Hill\, North Carolina\, 27514\, United States
CATEGORIES:Hike,Social,Training,Workshop
ORGANIZER;CN="Amaya Horner":MAILTO:ahorner@triangleland.org
END:VEVENT
